CHANGES MADE IN THIS EDITION
----------------------------

Relative to the upstream baseline imported in commit f4d6876 (2026-10-29).
CHANGELOG.md and `git log` record the changes in detail.

- Runtime: the NestJS API runs on Cloudflare Workers (apps/backend renamed
  to apps/api; Worker entry src/worker.ts; esbuild bundle build.mjs).
- Database: PostgreSQL replaced by Cloudflare D1 through Prisma 7 and its D1
  adapter; schema converted; new D1 migration history; per-restaurant write
  lock (Durable Object) in place of row locks.
- Realtime: Socket.IO replaced by a Durable Object WebSocket hub per
  restaurant and a browser WebSocket client.
- Storage and jobs: uploads, document attachments and backups moved to R2;
  timers replaced by Cron Triggers; logical D1 backups instead of pg_dump.
- E-mail: SMTP replaced by the Resend or SendGrid HTTPS APIs. PDF export moved
  from pdfkit to pdf-lib with an embedded Arabic font.
- Printing: USB thermal printing disabled on Workers; network printing over
  Cloudflare TCP sockets.
- Frontend hosting: Next.js built with OpenNext and served as a Worker that
  forwards /api to the API Worker over a service binding.
- Saudi edition: English/Arabic with RTL across the application; SAR,
  Asia/Riyadh and SA defaults; SA_VAT tax regime (15 % default, inclusive);
  ZATCA Phase 1 QR on simplified tax invoices; mada, STC Pay and Apple Pay
  payment methods; Arabic-first kiosk.
- Data migration tooling: PostgreSQL to D1/R2 export, transform, import and
  validation (scripts/migration).
- Interface redesign: new theme, navigation shell and UI primitives; screens
  reworked for mobile and tablet.
- Rebrand to Ahemad's Restro: new name, logo and icon set, central brand
  configuration (packages/types/src/brand.ts), package scope @ahemads-restro,
  renamed Workers and Cloudflare resources.
- New features: public marketing website in English and Arabic with SEO
  metadata, sitemap, robots, blog and legal pages; demo request endpoint and
  storage; adding branches from the application.
- Removed: self-hosted packaging (Docker, CasaOS, Windows MSIX, .deb,
  installer scripts), the Docker updater and their CI workflows. They remain
  available in the upstream repository.

Some identifiers from the upstream are kept unchanged for compatibility with
existing data, devices and integrations: the session cookie `nodedr_session`,
browser storage keys `nodedr-locale`, `nodedr-sidebar-collapsed`,
`nodedr_branch_id` and `nodedr_notifications_muted`, the customer-display
browser channel `orderrestro-customer-display`, webhook headers
`X-OrderRestro-*`, the backup format `orderrestro-d1/1`, and the order ticket
QR prefix `orderrestro:order:`.


